<h1 class="first">Executive Summary</h1>

<div class="exec-box">
  <p style="color:#FFC100; font-weight:bold; font-size:11pt; margin-bottom:8pt;">Strategic Overview</p>
  <p style="color:#CBD5E1; margin-bottom:8pt;">CampusOS has built a compelling all-in-one campus management platform gaining strong traction in the Indian higher education market. The product&#8217;s core value proposition &#8212; replacing 50+ disconnected tools with a unified LMS, SIS, Career Services CRM, attendance, and AI insights platform &#8212; maps directly to a massive, underserved pain point in North America.</p>
  <p style="color:#CBD5E1; margin:0;">However, the current positioning, terminology, compliance messaging, and SEO strategy are calibrated for Indian institutions and will create significant friction with North American buyers. This report outlines the strategic adjustments required to successfully enter the North American market.</p>
</div>

<h2>Key Findings</h2>
<div class="finding">
  <p style="margin-bottom:6pt;"><strong style="color:#0D1B2A;">1.</strong>&nbsp; The North American higher education software market exceeds <strong>$10 billion annually</strong></p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:6pt;"><strong style="color:#0D1B2A;">2.</strong>&nbsp; <strong>1,100+ community colleges</strong> represent an immediately accessible beachhead &#8212; underserved by overpriced legacy systems</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:6pt;"><strong style="color:#0D1B2A;">3.</strong>&nbsp; Current terminology (<strong>TnP CRM, NAAC accreditation, College ERP</strong>) is India-specific and will alienate North American buyers</p>
  <p style="margin-bottom:6pt;"><strong style="color:#0D1B2A;">4.</strong>&nbsp; <strong>FERPA compliance messaging</strong> is non-negotiable for US institutions and is currently absent</p>
  <p style="margin:0;"><strong style="color:#0D1B2A;">5.</strong>&nbsp; Competitor displacement messaging vs. <strong>Ellucian Banner and Blackboard</strong> represents a major SEO and positioning opportunity</p>
</div>

<h2>At a Glance</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th width="25%">Metric</th>
    <th width="25%">Figure</th>
